<title>MEXICO: FORECAST-Mexico 28-day Cetes seen up at 21.62 pct.</title>
<headline>FORECAST-Mexico 28-day Cetes seen up at 21.62 pct.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-03-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Interest rates on Mexico's bellwether 28-day Cetes, or T-bills, are seen rising 303 basis points to 21.62 percent, and rates are also seen rising at longer terms, according to a Reuters' survey of eight Cetes dealers.</p>
<p>Following is a table comparing last week's primary rates versus expectations for today's auction and the expected change in basis points.</p>
<p>    TERM	LAST WEEK    THIS WEEK'S SURVEY   CHANGE</p>
<p>    28-DAY     18.59	    21.62		  +303 bps</p>
<p>    91-DAY     21.18	    22.85		  +167 bps</p>
<p>    182-DAY    22.47	    23.56		  +109 bps</p>
<p>    1-YEAR     23.53	    24.26		   +72 bps</p>
<p>The results will be released by Banco de Mexico at 1830 EST/2330 GMT.</p>
<p>((- Mexico City newsroom +525 728-9559))</p>
